 Wayland clients in a Wayland desktop. That requires the Wayland server
 to be an X window manager as well.
 .TP 8
+.B \-surface-input-targets
+Route native Wayland pointer records through the entered surface's X window
+subtree. Requires \-rootless and is disabled by default. Target identity is
+preserved across synchronous grabs and replay, including surface destruction.
+XTEST, client pointer warps, touch, tablet and keyboard input retain their
+ordinary routing semantics.
+
+.TP 8
 .BI \-shm
 Force the shared memory backend instead of glamor (if available) for passing
 buffers to the Wayland server.
